    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.http_ingress_host", decl_name: "realize", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.http_ingress_host", decl_name: "realize_in", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.http_ingress_host", decl_name: "answer_with_handler", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.http_ingress_host", decl_name: "tests", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.serve_budget_refusal", decl_name: "json_string", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.http_ingress_host", decl_name: "INGRESS_MODULE", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.http_ingress_host", decl_name: "INGRESS_COPRODUCT", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.v1_interpreter", decl_name: "variant_arm_declarers", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.v1_interpreter", decl_name: "declared_parameter_names", field: WholeDeclaration }
  ],
  reason: "Binding a TCP or unix listener (a unix path only under its lock, held for the listener's lifetime, replacing only a socket shown stale), reading SO_PEERCRED off an accepted connection and resolving its uid, reading bytes within a limit, arming the interpreter's per-request evaluation budget around every evaluation one request's bytes depend on, and writing bytes are operations on a live connection and on the running interpreter that no .dag fold can perform. Everything those operations decide is evaluated in the loaded program: whether the binding's listener is one a socket can carry (http_ingress_listener_refusal, the fold the native door's start also consumes), the argument plan (http_ingress_fact_plan, from the handler's declared parameters, which declared_parameter_names reads because only the host holds the program), framing and limits (http_ingress_frame over native_serve_frame_within), the pre-evaluation route table and its bytes (http_ingress_pre_evaluation_routes, once at startup), the handler's arguments (http_ingress_arguments), what a read failure, handler error, budget refusal or non-response means (http_ingress_read_refused, http_ingress_handler_error, http_ingress_budget_refused, http_ingress_not_a_response), and the response head's bytes (http_ingress_outgoing, http_ingress_wire_head). The fold/fold_int/fold_text/str_list helpers only call those folds and read their answers. Whether an answer IS a binding is read by declaration identity: variant_arm_declarers exposes the interpreter's existing arm-to-declaring-coproduct index, because a runtime variant carries only spellings. json_string moved from cli_run with the budget refusal's machine body, which stays host-rendered because the evaluation that would render it is the one just aborted.",
  owning_dissolution_lane: "v1-hand-queue-drain" as RoadmapNodeId,
  trigger: "Delete all of these when every served deployment binding is realized natively: the native door carries the seed's whole handler contract (gunbc.plans.converged_ingress M2: request_headers, the attested unix-socket peer, the per-request budget, a native realization chosen in the binding) AND each served closure -- today the roadmap, fabric DB and approval broker handlers -- compiles on the native route, so no served deployment runs on the seed's interpreter. M2 alone does not fire this: it moves the device-crypto service only.",
  current_boundary: "Confined to cli_run::http_ingress_host, reached only from main.rs run_one_function when an entry's answer is an HttpIngressAdmission (never under --claim-run). It reads the request line and head lines within the binding's head limit and read timeout, matches the request line against the pre-evaluation table, reads exactly the body length the frame fold returns, and writes the bytes the response folds return. One request at a time, as the deleted seam was. Tests: cli_run::http_ingress_host::tests; parity claims: test.claim.http_ingress_witness; real route: the evaluation-budget falsifier host through test.fixture.serve_seam_ingress.",
}
